// M9A.3: whether a learner's developer profile can be seen without signing in.
// PRIVATE is the default and the only state an account is ever put in by the
// system; PUBLIC is set only by the owner, explicitly, from Settings. The profile
// page itself arrives in M9A.4 — until then this only records the choice.
//
// The columns live on User (example.prisma) rather than a new table: users already
// has row level security enabled with no policy, and nothing here is read through
// anything but the server's Prisma client (docs/rules/auth.md).
enum ProfileVisibility {
	PRIVATE
	PUBLIC
}
